  "narrative": {
    "intro": "The Department of the Interior obligated $378M in FY2027 to date. The Department of the Interior recorded 2,490 awards with an average award size of $152K, and obligations fell 94.5% year over year. Fiscal trends show a sharp drop in current-year obligations compared with recent full fiscal years: FY22 through FY26 obligations ranged from $6.5B to $8.1B, while FY27 to date stands at $378M. Computer Systems Design Services is the largest buying category in FY2027 to date at $195M, followed by construction and infrastructure-related categories such as Other Heavy and Civil Engineering Construction at $29.8M and Commercial and Institutional Building Construction at $25.1M. GUIDEHOUSE INC. is the largest vendor for FY2027 to date with $151M in obligations, and GENERAL DYNAMICS INFORMATION TECHNOLOGY, INC. is the second-largest with $33.7M. The fiscal snapshot shows concentrated spending in IT services and a set of construction and environmental services vendors receiving the majority of current-year obligations.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How does FY2027 to date compare with prior fiscal years?",
        "body": "The Department of the Interior obligated $378M in FY2027 to date, down 94.5% year over year. FY22 through FY26 obligations were $6.5B, $7.6B, $8.1B, $6.6B, and $6.8B respectively. The FY2027 total is a partial, fiscal year to date figure and is much smaller than any single prior full fiscal year listed."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Which vendors and contract categories dominate FY2027 to date?",
        "body": "GUIDEHOUSE INC. leads vendors with $151M in obligations, followed by GENERAL DYNAMICS INFORMATION TECHNOLOGY, INC. at $33.7M and PAULSEN CONSTRUCTION LLC at $21.6M. Computer Systems Design Services is the top NAICS category at $195M, with Other Heavy and Civil Engineering Construction at $29.8M and Commercial and Institutional Building Construction at $25.1M rounding out the next-largest categories."
      }
    ]
