  "faq": [
    {
      "q": "How much does Department of the Interior spend on contracts?",
      "a": "The Department of the Interior obligated $378M in FY2027 to date. The Department of the Interior recorded 2,490 awards with an average award size of $152K, and obligations fell 94.5% year over year. Full prior-year obligations were $6.5B in FY22, $7.6B in FY23, $8.1B in FY24, $6.6B in FY25, and $6.8B in FY26."
    },
    {
      "q": "What does Interior buy?",
      "a": "Interior buys a mix of IT services, construction, research, forestry support, and related services, led by Computer Systems Design Services at $195M. Other sizable FY2027 to date categories include Other Heavy and Civil Engineering Construction at $29.8M, Commercial and Institutional Building Construction at $25.1M, and Water and Sewer Line and Related Structures Construction at $21.4M."
    },
